%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2d56cce9b854dbe4eb4d220d3699184f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Plot_C0_S1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Client::PlotConfig
  chapterId: 0
  sceneId: 1
  nodes:
  - type: 0
    text: Welcome to the combat tutorial
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Now we will learn the basic mechanics
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: This is "instant", you can think of it as a fraction of time. A battle
      = 150 instants.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_1
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 60
  - type: 0
    text: 'It is just like an hour = 60 minutes, a second = 1000 miliseconds...

      Just
      different ways to calculate time, but all similar ideas.'
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_1
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'Now look at this bar over here: you can (and only can) command units that
      is on this bar when it''s your turn.'
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_2
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: And this bar is your opponent's bar, similar rule is applied.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_3
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Oh and when is your turn? Look over there, you can tell if the <u>Wait</u>
      button is visible.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: So yes, it is currently your turn. Click here to select your only available
      unit.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_5
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 2
    text: Perfect. On select a unit, you can select another <u>blue cell</u> as a
      target to move there. Click this cell first.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: -1}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Confirm your decision by clicking here.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_ConfirmButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 4
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Notice anything special? It is still your turn right?
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Dont worry, you are not breaking any rule. And the rule is really simple.
      Please look above, see the eyes? This is your eye.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_YourEye
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: -1}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: And this is your opponent's eye. Notice the difference yet?
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_EnemyEye
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: So yes, this is a turn-based game. The most obvious rule is each side take
      turns sequentially. But if one side's eye is closed, then that side no longer
      takes any turn. Simple right?
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'Also you can rest assured: an eye will not re-open if the instant hasn''t
      passed. Look: its still the same <u>instant</u> isn''t it?'
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_1
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: But when will the eyes open again? => The next <u>paused instant</u> if
      that side has <u>ready unit</u>.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: Then when is the next <u>paused instant</u>? => It is simple, after both
      sides closes the eyes, time flows again, and it will pause the <u>instant</u>
      when any new unit(s) enters the Ready Queue.
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 1
    text: Too much to handle? Dont worry just hit the <u>Wait button</u> and follow
      the tutorial, you will understand soon enough.
    tutorialTargetId: C0S1_WaitButton
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 13
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
  - type: 0
    text: 'Alot happened right? Eyes closed, opened, then closed.... So brief explanation:
      the bot for this tutorial auto skips its turn, and you can feel free to explore
      the game mechanism. (this explain the nearst eye closing)'
    tutorialTargetId: 
    targetCell: {x: 0, y: 0}
    delay: 0.5
    targetWaitTimeout: 10
